// ============================================================
// COMMAND / FEATURE REGISTRY  (Settings panel, MASTER PROMPT 5-6)
// ONE table owns every keyboard shortcut, every user-visible
// feature switch and the description of how each of them works.
// Nothing else may hardcode a binding: the dispatch chain, the
// hamburger-menu labels, the gear panel and the persistence all
// read THIS table, so a rebind or an OFF switch is picked up
// everywhere at once and can never drift out of sync.
//   EK_ACTION - has a shortcut that runs an action; `on` gates it
//   EK_OPTION - a real feature value in *var (switch = the value);
//               optional shortcut toggles it, key_gated = the key
//               must die together with the switch
//   EK_DOC    - documentation row only (fixed keys, no state)
// ============================================================

